{"source_id": "W3176543106", "title": "Low-Stakes Quizzes Improve Learning and Reduce Overconfidence in College Students", "year": 2021, "abstract": "Retrieval practice is a straightforward and effective way to improve student learning, and its efficacy has been demonstrated repeatedly in the laboratory and in the classroom. In the current study, we implemented retrieval practice in the form of low-stakes quizzes in an undergraduate course and compared quiz performance to rereading of assigned material. Students who completed the low-stakes quizzes performed better on subsequent unit exams than students who reread the material, and quizzing also reduced overconfidence relative to rereading. These findings suggest that low-stakes quizzing is a superior study strategy to rereading for improving exam performance in authentic classroom settings."}
